\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Arm of the Lord, awake, awake!
\par Thine own immortal strength put on;
\par With terror clothed, hell's kingdom shake,
\par And cast Thy foes with fury down.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As in the ancient days appear;
\par The sacred annals speak Thy fame:
\par Be now omnipotently near,
\par To endless ages still tha same.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy arm, Lord, is not shortened now,
\par It wants not now the power to save;
\par Still present with Thy people, Thou
\par Bear'st them through life's disparted wave.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. By death and hell pursued in vain,
\par To Thee the ransomed seed shall come;
\par Shouting, their heavenly zion gain,
\par And pass through death triumphant home.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

